<main class="zd-philosophy">

  <section class="zd-philosophy-hero">
    <div class="zd-philosophy-hero__bg">
      <img
        src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/aida/AP1WRLtDupvIqCn7Oki1maOG9NUaTJ2KK-L3IWxQfwCeaTvTYfT29HiqgLGuFBfeqR9CgBNgY-GAJ39r8HfeKtHnKmwVnPScXKKNDQgoGf5iycc1z8tQSqjJEAs0T3eEs7dZP93c8_CF6SaxF5YQMm0RBwBP7KqnHcXoUEp02Me82PNm6-ugpVQV2EsFSzSmHA39nclVZRloiOE3kuZj1NQLFAWrDKOll3SfIoe5FjXSCB3HpFaNXLJYu_sQMNdt"
        alt=""
        width="1800"
        height="1100"
      >
    </div>

    <div class="zd-philosophy-hero__content">
      <h1>Technology should serve your life, not <em>steal</em> it.</h1>
      <p>
        Ziyu Development is built around one belief: software should help people
        become more focused, intentional, capable, and present in real life.
      </p>

      <div class="zd-philosophy-actions">
        <a href="/pages/projects">Explore Projects</a>
        <a href="/pages/support">Support the Mission</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="zd-philosophy-split">
    <div>
      <p class="zd-philosophy-eyebrow">What is broken</p>
      <h2>Modern technology often rewards distraction.</h2>
    </div>

    <div>
      <p>
        We exist in an era of digital extraction. Apps compete for attention,
        notifications interrupt focus, and endless feeds make it easy to feel
        busy without becoming better.
      </p>

      <p>
        Ziyu Development exists to build the opposite: tools with purpose,
        boundaries, clarity, and a real-world reason to exist.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="zd-philosophy-principles">
    <div class="zd-philosophy-section-head">
      <p class="zd-philosophy-eyebrow">Core Principles</p>
      <h2>The beliefs behind every project.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="zd-philosophy-grid">
      <article>
        <span>01</span>
        <h3>Focus Over Noise</h3>
        <p>We prioritize deep work and singular focus. Interfaces should reduce distraction and let the primary task breathe.</p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <span>02</span>
        <h3>Real-Life Growth</h3>
        <p>Success is measured by who you become away from the app, not how long the app keeps you inside it.</p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <span>03</span>
        <h3>Clean Information</h3>
        <p>Information should be structured, legible, and useful. We avoid clutter in favor of clarity.</p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <span>04</span>
        <h3>Human Technology</h3>
        <p>Tools should respect human time, energy, attention, and emotion instead of exploiting them.</p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <span>05</span>
        <h3>Intentional Design</h3>
        <p>Every feature should have a reason. If it does not support the user’s goal, it should not be there.</p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <span>06</span>
        <h3>Build in Public</h3>
        <p>Transparency matters. We share progress, failures, lessons, and direction with the community.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="zd-philosophy-products">

  <div class="zd-philosophy-products__inner">

    <div class="zd-philosophy-products__head">
      <div>
        <p class="zd-philosophy-eyebrow">How it becomes real</p>
        <h2>Each product solves a different part of the same problem.</h2>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="zd-philosophy-product-list">

      <a href="/pages/goal-grower">
        <div>
          <h3>Goal Grower</h3>
          <p>Visual goal tracking inspired by gardens and long-term cultivation.</p>
        </div>
        <span>→</span>
      </a>

      <a href="/pages/myjourney">
        <div>
          <h3>MyJourney</h3>
          <p>A personal archive for documenting growth, experiences, and life milestones.</p>
        </div>
        <span>→</span>
      </a>

      <a href="/pages/blokkr">
        <div>
          <h3>Blokkr</h3>
          <p>A focus tool designed to reduce digital friction and protect attention.</p>
        </div>
        <span>→</span>
      </a>

      <a href="/pages/kindlitt">
        <div>
          <h3>Kindlitt</h3>
          <p>A calmer reading environment designed for deep learning and reflection.</p>
        </div>
        <span>→</span>
      </a>

    </div>

  </div>

</section>

  <section class="zd-philosophy-vision">
    <div class="zd-philosophy-vision__image">
